{"title":"Career Roadmap · Audiologist","role":"Audiologist","summary":"An Audiologist is a hearing and balance-care professional who evaluates auditory function, identifies hearing and related communication difficulties, provides rehabilitation, fits and manages hearing technology within professional scope, and supports patients and families through long-term hearing care.","facts":{"Current degree":"Allied Health Sciences (B.Sc / BPT / BOT / BMLT etc.)","Course":"Audiology & Speech-Language Pathology (BASLP)"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Career Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"An Audiologist is a hearing and balance-care professional who evaluates auditory function, identifies hearing and related communication difficulties, provides rehabilitation, fits and manages hearing technology within professional scope, and supports patients and families through long-term hearing care."},{"type":"p","text":"The career combines:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Audiological assessment"},{"text":"Ear and hearing physiology"},{"text":"Psychoacoustics"},{"text":"Diagnostic audiology"},{"text":"Hearing-aid technology"},{"text":"Cochlear-implant rehabilitation"},{"text":"Vestibular assessment"},{"text":"Pediatric audiology"},{"text":"Aural rehabilitation"},{"text":"Patient counselling"},{"text":"Clinical documentation"},{"text":"Digital hearing technologies"}]},{"type":"p","text":"A realistic pathway is:"},{"type":"flow","items":["BASLP","Clinical Audiology Training","Supervised Clinical Internship","Audiologist","Clinical Audiologist","Senior Audiologist","Audiology Specialist / Clinical Lead","Audiology Centre / Department Manager"]},{"type":"note","label":"Professional note","text":"Audiology is a regulated clinical profession. Registration, scope of practice and eligibility for independent clinical work should be verified against the current applicable professional requirements."}]},{"heading":"Career Horizons","kind":"h